Pin Pi test Node to prevent glibc drift

The cached Wolfi test image provides glibc 2.43, but installing nodejs
from the live APK repository now selects Node 26.8.1, which requires
GLIBC_2.44. APK accepts the installed libc, so npm fails before Pi can
be installed. The pinned Pi version does not pin its system Node
runtime.

Use the official Node 22.23.1 archive, matching the development
container, with committed SHA-256 checksums for x86_64 and aarch64. This
also pins the bundled npm and avoids the newer libc requirement of
Wolfi's Node build. Pi remains at 0.82.0 with its published
npm-shrinkwrap locking dependencies.

Validation: reproduced the original pi_smoke failure, then passed all
five Pi integration tests and enter_smoke_test,
enter_verifies_user_and_repo_path, claude_smoke, and
gateway_pod_commit_triggers_push through cargo pipeline. Formatting,
builds, and clippy also passed.
